\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Issue 4: Popup Runtime Connection Error (v1.0.0)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Problem:
\f1\b0  Console error when opening popup:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Unchecked runtime.lastError: Could not establish connection. \
Receiving end does not exist.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Root Cause:
\f1\b0  Popup tries to send message to content script even when user isn't on a Zendesk page.\

\f0\b Solution (v1.0.1):
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 chrome.tabs.query(\{ active: true, currentWindow: true \}, (tabs) => \{\
  if (tabs[0] && tabs[0].url && tabs[0].url.includes('zendesk.com')) \{\
    chrome.tabs.sendMessage(tabs[0].id, \{ action: 'getStatus' \}, (response) => \{\
      if (chrome.runtime.lastError) \{\
        console.log('Extension not active on this page yet');\
        return;\
      \}\
      // Process response\
    \});\
  \}\
\});\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Status:
\f1\b0  \uc0\u9989  RESOLVED in v1.0.1\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
